<Layout locale="en" title="Research partnerships — Astrmira" description="Work with Astrmira on shared scientific questions across data systems, efficient intelligence, and mathematics." route="projects/research-partnerships">
  <div class="wrap"><section class="page-title"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/en/" data-route="home">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/en/projects/" data-route="projects">Projects</a><span>/</span><span>Research partnerships</span></div><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH PARTNERSHIPS</p><h1>Let a good question<br /><em>meet shared curiosity.</em></h1><p>Research and university partnerships are a core direction. We connect our work in databases, retrieval, quantization, post-training, and mathematics to scientific questions that benefit from different kinds of experience.</p></section><article class="article-layout"><aside class="article-aside"><p class="eyebrow">JOINT RESEARCH</p><p>Research planning<br />Prototypes and evaluation</p></aside><div class="article-content"><h2>Begin with the question itself.</h2><p>Questions worth sustained study often need theoretical insight, experimental method, and systems experience together. A collaboration begins with the problem rather than a predetermined technical answer.</p><h2>Ways to work together.</h2><p>Joint problem selection, research prototypes, experimental evaluation, technical exchange, and paths toward practical use. Scope, ownership, and disclosure are agreed explicitly for each collaboration.</p><h2>How to begin.</h2><p>Bring a question, a research plan, or a cross-disciplinary challenge. We first discuss the goal, existing foundation, and what can be shared, then design an appropriate path.</p><p><a href="/en/collaborate/" class="button button-primary" data-route="collaborate">Discuss this direction <span class="arrow">↗</span></a></p></div></article></div>
</Layout>
